    "narrative": "The daily outlook for LawDog remains anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (77.97) and **Bryce Harper** (72.70), our two highest-rated options today. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is an elite start against Valdez, leveraging a significant +2% bump from the opponent's slow delivery, which creates an ideal environment for stealing bases\u2014a critical edge given our focus on the scarcest category. **Bryce Harper** enjoys a similarly favorable setup against P\u00e9rez, benefiting from a +4% park factor and an xwOBA of .394 that signals imminent production. Additionally, **Cal Raleigh** (74.07) is a must-start; while Springs presents a reasonable challenge, the combination of his #4 lineup spot and a +19% SP skill adjustment makes him our most efficient backstop play by a wide margin. **Daulton Varsho** (66.94) also deserves mention, as his +2% efficiency boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s delivery cadence aligns perfectly with his stolen base upside, making him a high-floor OF play.\n\nOn the bench, **Braden Montgomery** (42.58) was the closest cut from the starting nine. While his score remained above the 40-point threshold, he lacked the specific platoon or park-adjusted advantages that bolstered players like **Lawrence Butler** (61.72), who carries a superior +13% dynamic platoon edge today. **Alex Freeland** (38.20) failed to crack the lineup entirely, falling below our 40-point \"Zebras\" floor due to a daunting matchup against Cavalli and a poor SP skill adjustment (-17%). We continue to monitor the statuses of **Will Smith** and **Justin Crawford**, both of whom are unavailable today, leaving us to rely on the depth of **Dylan Beavers** (56.94) and **JJ Bleday** (45.87) to fill the gaps.\n\nRisk management remains a priority for the late-season stretch. While **Jonathan Aranda** (50.72) is a marginal start, his exposure to the elite arm of deGrom (3.15 xERA) carries significant volatility; if his lineup position shifts, we may see his efficiency drop further. Furthermore, while we are confident in the projected production for **Gleyber Torres** and **Luis Arraez**, both are facing southpaws in Messick and P\u00e9rez respectively. We are banking on the dynamic platoon adjustments to carry these hitters, but any unexpected weather or defensive shifts could quickly compress their expected scoring. With **Matt Chapman**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Tyler Freeman**, and **Kyle Karros** also on the roster, we remain positioned to adjust if these starters underperform or if conditions shift mid-game.",
